# Complexity

When an authoritative complexity checker exists, satisfy it for the touched functions. That is a number, not a vibe. Existing debt stays unless the task requires it.

- Cyclomatic: repo rule when present (MEASURED). When no linter exists (UNMEASURED), prefer flat control flow and early returns; do not guess a score. Never above **22**; a stricter repo cap wins. Above 22 needs an explicit user exception the agent cannot invent.
- Cognitive: only when this repo already measures it (Sonar / sonarjs); use that cap or **22**, whichever is tighter. Do not add Sonar.
- Halstead difficulty: only when already measured; **< 80**. Do not add a Halstead tool.
- CRAP: only when already measured; **< 25**. Do not add a CRAP reporter.
- Do not disable cyclomatic lint to hide findings (`eslint-disable` complexity, `# noqa: C901`, `--ignore C901`, clippy allow). A legitimate config fix needs a one-line why.
- Extract; early return; flat `if`. Nesting compliance does not excuse high cyclomatic complexity.
- Done = cited lint green (analyzer + cap + scope) when a job exists; otherwise report unmeasured, never claim green.

## Procedure
When the repo has no cap or lint is red, read `shared/skills/complexity/SKILL.md`.
